  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nSunday looks slightly cooler than Saturday, especially in Oregon \nzones, as part of the upper trough off the northwest coast moves \ninland across WA.  Most of our CWA will be sunny and dry but monsoon \nmoisture will still clip south-central Idaho, with a slight boost \nfrom Hurricane Fausto as it heads westward across the subtropical \nPacific. Forecast has a 15 percent chance of thunderstorms in Twin \nFalls County Sunday. Monday through Wednesday should be dry in all \nareas and several degrees cooler than previous days, as more of the \nupper trough off the northwest coast comes inland.",
